INT. SKATE SHOP BACKROOM - NIGHT

Stacked decks. A mini fridge. A busted couch. A radio on the shelf mutters traffic.

DEVONTE "DEV" MWANGI (17, bleached hair, scraped elbows) tapes grip onto a board. TESSA PRZYBYLSKI (17, overalls, zine in her back pocket) sits cross-legged on the couch. JUN-HO CHOI (18, nervous, backpack on) stands by the door. MARCELLINE "MARCY" ROUSSEAU (16, thrift-store blazer) hunches beside the fridge, phone in hand.

TESSA
Okay, Dev. Jun-ho wants to say something.

DEV
Then he can say it.

JUN-HO
I... got in.

TESSA
Got in where?

JUN-HO
Seoul. Design school. The letter came today.

DEV
Dude. That's huge.

MARCY
When do you leave?

JUN-HO
August.

TESSA
Jun-ho, that's like two months.

JUN-HO
Two and a half.

DEV
Marcy, tell him it's cool.

MARCY
(flat)
It's cool.

DEV
See? Cool.

JUN-HO
You don't think I'm abandoning you?

TESSA
Jun-ho, you're the only one who can actually draw.

DEV
Tessa.

TESSA
What? It's true. The rest of us just push wood.

MARCY
My phone's buzzing.

DEV
Answer it.

MARCY
It's my mom. She'll just ask where I am.

DEV
So tell her.

MARCY
(answering, bright)
Hi, Maman. At Dev's. No. No, I'm eating. Okay. Okay. Love you.

She hangs up. Everyone looks at her.

MARCY (CONT'D)
What?

TESSA
Marcy. You haven't eaten since lunch.

MARCY
I'm not hungry.

DEV
You said that at lunch.

JUN-HO
I'll get pizza.

MARCY
Don't.

JUN-HO
Marcy.

MARCY
I said don't!

The radio crackles. A voice leaks through.

RADIO ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
...and that's the weather. Tomorrow clear, with a high of seventy-eight...

DEV
We should go skate. The lot's empty.

TESSA
It's ten at night.

DEV
So it's empty.

JUN-HO
I'm in.

MARCY
(after a long beat)
Fine. But I'm not wearing a helmet.

TESSA
Marcy.

MARCY
Fine, fine. A helmet.

Dev grins. He tosses the board to Jun-ho.
